  "first_shell_residue_counts_available": false,
  "limitations": [
    "Slot 0 counts candidate residue-metal pairs, not unique first-shell residues or certified coordination bonds; a bridging residue may count once for each center.",
    "Candidates use at most two listed donor atoms per residue and retain the nearest one per residue-metal pair; when no listed donor is present, the functional-group centroid is used.",
    "The 2.7 Angstrom candidate cutoff has a first-shell override for the nearest center; site statistics do not force a candidate for every metal.",
    "Waters, cofactors, and noncanonical residues are omitted; intra-residue bidentate angles are absent.",
    "Angles are formed within each metal center and then pooled across centers; site-level summaries lose per-center distributions.",
    "Zero angle pairs mean the six angular slots are padding zeros, not observed zero-degree angles. Positive pair count alone does not prove chemically valid or nondegenerate bond geometry.",
    "The 90/180 deviation is an ideal-angle proxy and cannot distinguish square-planar from octahedral coordination.",
    "Diagnostics do not identify donor-versus-centroid frequency, unique first-shell residue counts, per-center counts, cutoff overrides, or degenerate vectors; those quantities cannot be recovered from these eight slots.",
    "All reported angle-summary distributions weight pockets equally and condition on positive angle-pair count; they are not pooled individual-angle distributions.",
    "These diagnostics come from the A actual-data preflight. Candidate counts need not equal metal-node graph edge counts, which can force a nearest candidate for an otherwise disconnected center."
  ],
